  "narrative": "I audited the 12 new discovery results (R13-R24) for direction, clinical scale, precision, and multiplicity. All analyses had adequate cell sizes, and estimates are already signed to their registered directions. Using a 10% threshold on the absolute population mean outcome scale, no new interval excludes zero, so none can be accepted as a confirmed dataset-specific association. Two results have signed upper bounds below the relevant 10% reference and therefore fail even a permissive clinical-plausibility screen: H14 for feature_002/outcome_011 (signed estimate -0.0126, upper +0.0105, reference about 0.0301) and H16 for feature_002/outcome_013 (signed estimate +0.0036, upper +0.0235, reference about 0.0269). I reject and close these because meaningful support in the registered direction is ruled out. I also reassessed H10 as rejected and closed: the registered negative interaction for feature_002/outcome_006 in the high feature_018 group is not supported, and the simple-effect decomposition shows the signal in the complement (H20/R19), not in the claimed subgroup. The most clinically promising new result is H20: within feature_018 <= 0.9554, feature_002 has a signed association estimate of +0.0374 for outcome_006, about 2.1 times the 10% reference of about 0.0175, though the interval still includes zero and opposite values. I request independent validation for H20 because this is the only new comparison with a central estimate clearly above the clinical threshold and with adequate cells. Other borderline results remain deferred rather than active. H15 (feature_002/outcome_008) and H22 (feature_045/outcome_012 overall) have positive signed estimates but fall below their 10% references and are imprecise. H17 suggests the earlier feature_045 signal is not specific to feature_009 level_003, while H22 shows a similar overall magnitude; thus I do not pursue the context-specific version further. The outcome_014 follow-ups (H18, H21, H23, H24, H25) are too imprecise or near zero to support associations, despite the smaller absolute mean giving a lower absolute 10% reference. The feature_002 high-feature_018 simple effect (H19) is tiny. These conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset only; validation of H20 will only indicate whether that subgroup-specific association holds on independent data, not causality or broader generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Round 2 appraisal: no accepted claims. Rejected/closed: H10, H14, H16. Active unresolved candidate: H20 (feature_002/outcome_006 in low feature_018 group), with signed estimate 0.0374 vs threshold about 0.0175; independent validation requested. Deferred unresolved: H15, H17, H18, H19, H21, H22, H23, H24, H25. Feature_002 is not coherently associated across outcomes; H2 and H20 are outcome/subgroup-specific and remain tentative. Feature_045/outcome_012 has borderline estimates overall and in level_003 but central magnitude below 10%; defer unless validation or a stronger follow-up emerges. Outcome_014 tests are noisy or null. Next synthesis must immediately reassess H20 after validation: accept only if validation estimate and independent interval are clinically meaningful in the registered direction; otherwise reject/defer H20. Do not validate H10 again; if H20 validates and a modification claim remains interesting, a reversed interaction could be considered as a new proposal with proper caution about data-driven direction.",
